I walk into my new flat.
It is small, but it is bright.
I put my bag on the floor.
I walk slowly around the room.
I open the curtains.
The winter light fills the room.
A sofa stands by the wall.
A small table stands by the window.
And a bed stands in the corner.
There is a small rug lying under the table.
The flat is simple.
It is very quiet here.
My things are not here yet.
But everything is good.
It is my flat.
It feels just right.
